			   DATA_TYPE POLYBENCH_2D(path,N,N,n,n))
{
  int i, j, k;

  /* Tiling factors for the i (row) and j (column) dimensions.
   *
   * Rationale:
   *   - path is stored row-major, so j is the naturally vectorizable,
   *     unit-stride dimension.
   *   - Working on TI×TJ tiles improves cache locality for both path[i][j]
   *     and the k-th row path[k][j].
   *   - Values are chosen conservatively; they do not need to divide n.
